What is Carbomer?
Carbomer is a high-molecular-weight polymer of acrylic acid that's cross-linked with polyalkenyl ethers. Typically appearing as a white, fluffy powder, this compound serves as a critical viscosity-increasing agent and stabilizer in numerous formulations. Best recognized for its use in cosmetics, carbomer also has significant utility in medicine and hygiene products. Most regulatory bodies regard various carbomer types as safe for use, though some neutralizing agents required for pH adjustment may present formulation challenges in certain contexts.

